version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ShifatSahariar/SpreadEx"
abstract: >-
  SpreadEx runs several grammar-based input generators against a compiler,
  interpreter or parser, compares them by Cluster Coverage on a shared
  embedding-based diversity map, and spends a limited execution budget on the
  most diverse inputs first. A local browser Workbench and a CLI share one
  campaign engine; every campaign is recorded and can be replayed.
keywords:
  - grammar-based testing
  - fuzzing
  - test generator selection
  - test input prioritization
  - input diversity
  - compiler testing
